================================================================================
Third-party code inside the V8 static library
================================================================================

oam links a PREBUILT V8 static library, supplied by the `v8` crate. That crate
declares itself MIT -- which covers its Rust bindings -- and ships no license
files at all, so `cargo about` reports only "v8: MIT" and cannot see anything
compiled into the library itself. The section above covers V8 proper; this one
covers the third-party code V8 bundles, which is redistributed in every oam
binary and carries its own terms.

That the code is genuinely present was verified against a shipped binary rather
than inferred: `oam.exe` contains 2794 `icu` markers and ICU timezone data
(`Etc/GMT`), and `process.versions.icu` reports a real ICU version.

Components, and the license each is taken under. Where a component offers a
choice, the Apache-2.0 arm is selected, consistent with oam's own license:

